  "question": {
    "text": "A train of length <math><mi>L</mi></math> move with a constant speed <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> A person at the back of the train fires a bullet at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> towards a target which is at a distance of <math><mi>D</mi></math> (at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> ) from the front of the train (on the same direction of motion). Another person at the front of the train fires another bullet at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></math> towards the same target. Both bullets reach the target at the same time. Assuming the speed of the bullets <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></math> are same, the length of the train is"
  },
